-- title:
--   Transport of extra level structures along a rigidification
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfel'd frame for fake elliptic curves, and the hypotheses fall into the blocks listed below; each block is named and its content is summarised.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$, and a non-zero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   *Coefficient rings.* A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi\in\mathcal O$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the ideal $(\pi)$, the condition $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ and the equality of ideals $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hdvr`, `hπ`, `hcomplete`, `hres`, `hunr`), together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. A further characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, each element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, each monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ having a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`, `hOnr_alg`, `hOnr_closed`, `hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   *Indefinite side and moduli.* Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`), and a coarse moduli datum: a scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, a point assignment `pt` sending a ring $S$, an $\mathcal O$-point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec}S$ and a fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure over $S$ to a point of $\mathcal X$ over $s$, and `h𝒳` asserting that this datum is a coarse moduli space (isomorphism-invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property).
--
--   *Auxiliary full level and twisting.* An integer $n\ge 3$ coprime to $N$ and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$; a fine moduli scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with full level-$n$ structure with point assignment `ptF` (`hM`); a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ realising the level twists (`hρ`); and a forgetful morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`).
--
--   *Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner data.* For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with an extra level at $\ell$ (`h𝒴`), with two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1$ to $\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) computing, on points, the curve itself and the quotient by a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₀`, `hd₁`); endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   *Definite side.* Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`), an adelic element $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ with $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hn₁`, `hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, the place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$, the group $\Gamma^{t}$ of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ integral for $R_1$ away from $v$ (`hΓt`), families $s_\ell$, $sf_\ell$ satisfying the four conditions of `hs` (local agreement away from $r$, triviality at $r$, membership of $\ell\,sf_\ell^{-1}$ in the level Hecke set or the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ according as $\ell\mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and an element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   *The base curve over the residue ring.* The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$; a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$ (values in the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$) which is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, obeys the twisted multiplication rule of `IsOrderCoord`, is injective, has dense image modulo every power of $r$ and matches reduced traces (`hcoord`); a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ with formal coordinates $\theta_0$ presenting the formal group of $A_0$ through $\mathrm{coord}$ (`hX₀`, `hA₀`), a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$, and an Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on $A_0$: $A_{0w}$, morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and an exponent $k_w$ with `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (a single conjugator $g$ matching the formal actions of the $e_\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and of $a_w\!\cdot\! b_w$ with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to powers of $r$).
--
--   *The $\Gamma^t$- and order-actions on $A_0$.* Endomorphism families $e,e'$ with degrees $\deg$ and the hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (isogeny pairs of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level, multiplicativity and the scalar rules up to $r$-powers, the converse characterisation of scalars, compatibility of the $e_\gamma$ with the formal module through $\iota_0$ up to $r$-powers, labelling of the level-$n$ structure, and the statement that every $r$-power isogeny of a geometric fibre pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$); an order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators and a family $\hat e$ of endomorphisms subject to `hE5a`–`hE5e`, `hE5g` (additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation, unitality, multiplicativity, the integer case, $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, comparison with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$, joint compatibility with the formal module, and stability of $R_2$ under the main involution); the twin maximal order $\Lambda_{1s}$ with $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$, an order $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ containing $R_2$ with $r$-power denominators, and a family $\hat e'$ subject to `hE6a`–`hE6f` (the analogous multiplicative, involutive and norm identities, agreement with $\hat e$ on $R_2$, faithfulness, and the criterion `hE6f` detecting divisibility by a prime $q\neq r$ from the action on $q$-torsion).
--
--   *The formal moduli problem.* A ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition (`hMD`), a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$ with the three clauses of `hη` (injectivity up to isomorphism on admissible objects, naturality, and local surjectivity), and an injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the actions on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ with bounded denominators (`hE₀`). A comparison $eD$ identifying the functor $G_{\mathcal O}(MD)$ with the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ and the Deligne functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$, natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the leg $\psi$ (`hfstD`), translating the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), translating $\pi$-translation into Frobenius twisting of the leg (`hPiD`), and admitting $\pi$-translates (`hPiexD`). A homomorphism $\kappa:O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), together with an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed forward along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   *The Drinfel'd functor on rigidified curves.* A map $\Xi$ assigning to every rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent a point of $G_{\mathcal O}(MD)$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected bases the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of curve and rigidification), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms matched by the rigidifications up to $r$-powers) and `hΞdef` (computation of $\Xi$ through $\eta$ and a rigidified transport of $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with $j\le 1$).
--
--   *Equivariance of $\Xi$.* An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and the hypotheses `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (when $\bar r$ is invertible), and passing along a level-$\ell$ isogeny (under the Hecke data and joint compatibility conditions spelled out in `heqS`) correspond, under $\Xi$, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ and of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$ respectively, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$.
--
--   *The uniformisation datum.* A homomorphism $\theta^t:\Gamma^t\to G$ and a comparison $\Theta_f$ from the product of $\mathrm{corep}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\times\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ with the constant functor $G$ to the nilpotent points of $f_M$, subject to `hnat` (naturality), `hG` (equivariance for the $G$-action on $M$), `hi'` (invariance under the twisted action of $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ combined with $\theta^t\gamma$), `het` (unique lifting along surjections whose kernel multiplies to zero) and `hfib` (description of the fibres of $\Theta_f$ over algebraically closed fields by $\Gamma^t$-orbits, with the Frobenius twist prescribed by $\mathrm{vdet}$).
--
--   *The comparison clauses.* `hC0e` and `hC0u`: existence and uniqueness of the points of a normalised level transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification. `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`: existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism matched by the rigidifications, and pullback of a rigidified curve realising a given Deligne datum under $eD\circ\Xi$ twisted by $g_0^{-1}$. `hC2`: the point of $M$ produced by $\Theta_f$ at $(\psi,P)$ and $1\in G$ is the point `ptF` of the curve with its transported full level structure. `hC3`: for $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ acting on the Deligne datum, existence of a second rigidification of the same curve realising the new datum, such that the transported full level structures differ by the twist $\chi(\theta^t\gamma)$ and such that extra levels at primes $\ell\neq r$ (invertible in $B$) transported from a $\Gamma^t$-stable extra level of $A_0$ through the two rigidifications have the same points. `hC4` and `hC4pi`: the same for a general unit $h$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ and for $\pi$-translation. `hC5`: over an algebraically closed field, two rigidifications of isomorphic curves realising data $P$, $P'$ are related by some $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$, the isomorphism carries the $\chi(\theta^t\gamma)$-twist of one transported level structure to the other, and an extra level at $\ell$ matches across the isomorphism exactly when the corresponding extra level of $A_0$ is stable under $e_\gamma$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Both assertions are quantified over a Noetherian commutative ring $B$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with level-$N$ structure, a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ with respect to $A_0$ over the Frobenius twist $\mathrm{frobTwist}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\mathrm{Fr}\,(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))\,\psi$ — thus $\varrho$ consists of a reduction $\varrho.E_b$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$ with its comparison $\varrho.g_b$, a pullback $\varrho.A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg with its comparison $\varrho.g_A$, and an isogeny pair $\varrho.\varphi,\varrho.\varphi'$ of degree $r^{\varrho.d}$ from $\varrho.E_b$ to $\varrho.A_b$ preserving the level structure — a prime $\ell\neq r$ whose image in $B$ is a unit, and an extra level $K_0$ of $A_0$ at $\ell$.
--
--   First conjunct (existence): there is an extra level $C$ of $E$ at $\ell$ such that for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t':T\to\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)$ and every point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$, if the composite $R\cdot\varrho.g_b$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$, that is if there is $R_0:T\to C.K$ with $R_0$ followed by $C.\mathrm{levK}$ equal to $R$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$, then there is $Q_0:T\to K_0.K$ with $Q_0$ followed by $K_0.\mathrm{levK}$ equal to $R$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ and then by $\varrho.g_A$.
--
--   Second conjunct (uniqueness of the points): for any two extra levels $C,C'$ of $E$ at $\ell$ both satisfying the displayed condition with respect to the same $K_0$ and the same $\varrho$, and for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}B$ and every point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, the point $R$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$ if and only if it factors through $C'.\mathrm{levK}$. Uniqueness is thus asserted at the level of points, not as an equality of the two extra level structures.
--
--   This is the transport of an extra level structure at an auxiliary prime $\ell\neq r$ from the base fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over the residue ring to a rigidified curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent base, in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of the Shimura curve and its Hecke tower: existence of the transported level at $\ell$, and uniqueness of its points. It feeds the construction of the tower family of lifts over the Drinfel'd frame, used in the level-lowering part of the argument.
